# Build context for the frontend image (docker-compose.local.yml -> context: ./quorumtrading-frontend).
#
# Without this file the context is 3.1 GB, nearly all of it node_modules and .next that the build
# immediately discards and regenerates. That is the single biggest cost in the "all you need is
# Docker" first run the README advertises.
#
# node_modules is not just weight, it is a correctness bug. The Dockerfile does:
#     COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules      # linux, installed by npm ci
#     COPY . .                                               # <- host node_modules lands on top
# so a macOS-built tree silently overwrites the linux one, and the platform-specific optional
# dependencies no longer match the image. Excluding it is what makes `npm ci` in the deps stage
# mean anything.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Local env. `next build` reads .env.local, so leaving it in the context bakes whatever a
# developer happens to have locally into the image. The compose stack passes no NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# build args on purpose — it relies on the built-in default base URL. A committed .env.production
# is still honoured.
.env
.env*.local
.env.local.backup
.env.local.profile

# Test and coverage artifacts, none of which belong in an image
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
playwright/.cache
# Saved Playwright session state — real auth cookies for the e2e user
.playwright

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Never needed at build time
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
